 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios Global Payments shares spiked nearly 10% on Friday, after private equity firm GTCR confirmed in a regulatory filing that it's working on a take-private bid.

 GTCR holds a 16.35% stake in Global Payments. It received the shares earlier this year via the $24.25 billion sale of Worldpay to Global Payments. The deal reportedly could be valued at around $50 billion, although GTCR would need partners. There had been reports that CD&amp;R was a possibility, but it seems to have since backed away. Axios Pro's Ryan Lawler: "Global Payments shares had fallen since the Worldpay deal, and perhaps GTCR believes the market is underestimating what the combined business will do once fully integrated. Or that it could do a better job on the integration."

 
 
